cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "world-maps: testing video-model internals against human physical perception"
message: "If you reference this software, please cite the repository and the original studies whose data it uses."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Physical Reasoning
repository-code: "https://github.com/physicalreasoning/world-maps"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - intuitive physics
  - video models
  - world models
  - human-model comparison
  - event perception
abstract: >-
  Exploratory analyses of public data from the Yale Cognitive and Neural Computation Lab.
  Compares video-model prediction error and representation change with human detection of
  slowdowns around physical-event boundaries, and reanalyzes Woven's agreement with human
  cloth judgments. Confirmatory studies are planned and not yet run.
